course: dictionary
lesson: 6864
title: Too sure of yourself
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Overconfident means too sure of yourself. Being confident is good, but overconfident means you believe in yourself so much that you stop trying properly. «The hare was sure he would win, so he stopped to nap.» The hare thinks he cannot lose, so he does not prepare or take the race seriously.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Sure, risks and not preparing all point to believing in yourself too much. Test your meaning: "The team was too sure of itself and did not practise" still makes sense, so overconfident must mean too sure.
explain: The Bible's Book of Proverbs says, «Those who flatter their neighbours are spreading nets for their feet.» Empty praise can make people overconfident, and then they walk straight into trouble, like someone stepping into a net they cannot see.
fact: Confident means you believe in yourself. Overconfident means you believe too much, more than is sensible.
fact: Overconfident people may take risks or skip practice because they think they will succeed anyway.
fact: In «The Tortoise and the Hare», the hare was overconfident, and this warns the reader that he may fail.
fact: Praise that is empty, or not earned, can make a person overconfident.
fact: A good check is to swap in "too sure of yourself" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The hare was overconfident, so he did not hurry.» What does overconfident mean? | Very quick to finish | *Too sure of yourself, so you do not prepare | Afraid of every race | Kind to all the other animals
exercise: Maya says the swimmer was overconfident because he skipped training. Why does she say this? | *He was too sure he would win, so he did not practise | He was nervous before the race | He was very polite to the judges | He trained every day for a year
exercise: Which sentence shows someone being overconfident? | "I asked my coach for tips." | "I am nervous, but I will try my best." | *"I'm sure I'll win, so I won't bother to revise." | "I checked my answers twice, just to be safe."
test: «The hare thought he could win without trying, so he lay down to sleep.» Which word describes the hare's attitude? | Polite | Afraid | *Overconfident | Lazy and sad
test: According to the lesson, what can empty praise do to a person? | Makes them cry | Makes them quieter | Makes them forget how to speak | *Can make them overconfident
exam: Which best explains why overconfident people can fail? | They always ask for help | They never take part | *They stop preparing because they think they will win anyway | They try too hard in every game
